``` Detection: Password spraying (MITRE ATT&CK T1110.003)
    Data: Windows Security Event 4625 (failed logon), forwarded from DC01/WS01.
    Logic: one source attempting a small number of passwords against MANY distinct accounts in a
    short window - the inverse of brute force. The threshold is tuned to the lab (>= 5 distinct
    targets in 10 minutes from one source); bump distinct_users for a noisier environment.
    Status/Sub_Status 0xC000006A = bad password, 0xC0000234 = account locked. ```
index=winlogs source="WinEventLog:Security" EventCode=4625
| bin _time span=10m
| stats dc(Account_Name) as distinct_users
        values(Account_Name) as targeted_accounts
        count as failed_logons
        values(Sub_Status) as sub_status
        by _time, Workstation_Name, Source_Network_Address
| where distinct_users >= 5
| sort - distinct_users
